      "statement": "The S2–S4 hole–electron overlap analysis is reported with stable state-resolved Sr values under the benchmark validation protocol.",
      "expected": "Benchmark-computed Sr(S2)=0.91366, Sr(S3)=0.74133, Sr(S4)=0.74956 from Gaussian B3LYP/6-311G(d,p) S0 optimization and six vertical full-TDDFT singlet states, coefficients printed down to 1e-4, followed by Multiwfn 2026.7.15 high grid (1782000 points), cfgcrossthres=0.01. S2/S3 were additionally checked at cfgcrossthres=0.001 on the same high grid; all four states were checked at 0.001 on medium grid. Match each physical state, not an arbitrary row. These are benchmark references accepted by the user, not a reproduction of SI Table S11. The authored absolute allowance is 0.08, consistent with the existing S1 Sr rule; this is not a claim that every electronic-structure method agrees within that interval.",
